is the world's largest religion, with over two billion adherents, and it began in the first century with Jesus of Nazareth, a Jewish preacher crucified in Jerusalem around AD 30-33, whose followers proclaimed that he rose from the dead.\"},{\"text\":\"Christianity began in the first century with Jesus of Nazareth.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"Christianity is the world's largest religion, with over two billion adherents, and it began in the first century with Jesus of Nazareth, a Jewish preacher crucified in Jerusalem around AD 30-33, whose followers proclaimed that he rose from the dead.\"},{\"text\":\"Jesus of Nazareth was a Jewish preacher.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"Christianity is the world's largest religion, with over two billion adherents, and it began in the first century with Jesus of Nazareth, a Jewish preacher crucified in Jerusalem around AD 30-33, whose followers proclaimed that he rose from the dead.\"},{\"text\":\"Jesus of Nazareth was crucified in Jerusalem around AD 30-33.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"Christianity is the world's largest religion, with over two billion adherents, and it began in the first century with Jesus of Nazareth, a Jewish preacher crucified in Jerusalem around AD 30-33, whose followers proclaimed that he rose from the dead.\"},{\"text\":\"The followers of Jesus of Nazareth proclaimed that he rose from the dead.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"Christianity is the world's largest religion, with over two billion adherents, and it began in the first century with Jesus of Nazareth, a Jewish preacher crucified in Jerusalem around AD 30-33, whose followers proclaimed that he rose from the dead.\"},{\"text\":\"Monotheism is a central belief of Christianity.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Its central beliefs are monotheism, the Trinity (God as Father, Son (Jesus), and the Holy Spirit), the incarnation and divinity of Jesus, and salvation by God's grace through faith in Christ's death and resurrection.\"},{\"text\":\"The Trinity, God as Father, Son (Jesus), and the Holy Spirit, is a central belief of Christianity.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Its central beliefs are monotheism, the Trinity (God as Father, Son (Jesus), and the Holy Spirit), the incarnation and divinity of Jesus, and salvation by God's grace through faith in Christ's death and resurrection.\"},{\"text\":\"The incarnation and divinity of Jesus is a central belief of Christianity.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Its central beliefs are monotheism, the Trinity (God as Father, Son (Jesus), and the Holy Spirit), the incarnation and divinity of Jesus, and salvation by God's grace through faith in Christ's death and resurrection.\"},{\"text\":\"Salvation by God's grace through faith in Christ's death and resurrection is a central belief of Christianity.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Its central beliefs are monotheism, the Trinity (God as Father, Son (Jesus), and the Holy Spirit), the incarnation and divinity of Jesus, and salvation by God's grace through faith in Christ's death and resurrection.\"},{\"text\":\"The sacred text of Christianity is the Bible.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Its sacred text is the Bible, made up of the Old (Hebrew) and New (Greek) Testaments, which Christians regard as the inspired and authoritative Word of God.\"},{\"text\":\"The Bible is made up of the Old (Hebrew) and New (Greek) Testaments.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Its sacred text is the Bible, made up of the Old (Hebrew) and New (Greek) Testaments, which Christians regard as the inspired and authoritative Word of God.\"},{\"text\":\"Christians regard the Bible as the inspired and authoritative Word of God.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Its sacred text is the Bible, made up of the Old (Hebrew) and New (Greek) Testaments, which Christians regard as the inspired and authoritative Word of God.\"},{\"text\":\"Baptism as a rite of initiation is a core practice of Christianity.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Core practices include baptism as a rite of initiation, the Eucharist (communion) commemorating Jesus' last supper, prayer, and communal worship in a church.\"},{\"text\":\"The Eucharist (communion) is a core practice of Christianity.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Core practices include baptism as a rite of initiation, the Eucharist (communion) commemorating Jesus' last supper, prayer, and communal worship in a church.\"},{\"text\":\"The Eucharist commemorates Jesus' last supper.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Core practices include baptism as a rite of initiation, the Eucharist (communion) commemorating Jesus' last supper, prayer, and communal worship in a church.\"},{\"text\":\"Prayer is a core practice of Christianity.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Core practices include baptism as a rite of initiation, the Eucharist (communion) commemorating Jesus' last supper, prayer, and communal worship in a church.\"},{\"text\":\"Communal worship in a church is a core practice of Christianity.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Core practices include baptism as a rite of initiation, the Eucharist (communion) commemorating Jesus' last supper, prayer, and communal worship in a church.\"},{\"text\":\"Over the centuries Christianity divided into three main branches: Catholicism, Eastern Orthodoxy, and Protestantism.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Over the centuries the faith divided into three main branches - Catholicism, Eastern Orthodoxy (split in the East-West Schism of 1054), and Protestantism (emerging from the 16th-century Reformation and itself split into hundres or thousands different sects) - and today it is growing fastest in Africa and Asia while declining in much of the Western world.\"},{\"text\":\"Eastern Orthodoxy split in the East-West Schism of 1054.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Over the centuries the faith divided into three main branches - Catholicism, Eastern Orthodoxy (split in the East-West Schism of 1054), and Protestantism (emerging from the 16th-century Reformation and itself split into hundres or thousands different sects) - and today it is growing fastest in Africa and Asia while declining in much of the Western world.\"},{\"text\":\"Protestantism emerged from the 16th-century Reformation.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Over the centuries the faith divided into three main branches - Catholicism, Eastern Orthodoxy (split in the East-West Schism of 1054), and Protestantism (emerging from the 16th-century Reformation and itself split into hundres or thousands different sects) - and today it is growing fastest in Africa and Asia while declining in much of the Western world.\"},{\"text\":\"Protestantism is split into hundres or thousands different sects.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Over the centuries the faith divided into three main branches - Catholicism, Eastern Orthodoxy (split in the East-West Schism of 1054), and Protestantism (emerging from the 16th-century Reformation and itself split into hundres or thousands different sects) - and today it is growing fastest in Africa and Asia while declining in much of the Western world.\"},{\"text\":\"Christianity today is growing fastest in Africa and Asia.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Over the centuries the faith divided into three main branches - Catholicism, Eastern Orthodoxy (split in the East-West Schism of 1054), and Protestantism (emerging from the 16th-century Reformation and itself split into hundres or thousands different sects) - and today it is growing fastest in Africa and Asia while declining in much of the Western world.\"},{\"text\":\"Christianity today is declining in much of the Western world.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Over the centuries the faith divided into three main branches - Catholicism, Eastern Orthodoxy (split in the East-West Schism of 1054), and Protestantism (emerging from the 16th-century Reformation and itself split into hundres or thousands different sects) - and today it is growing fastest in Africa and Asia while declining in much of the Western world.\"}]}","ttft_ms":21944,"type":"result","duration_ms":21981,"uuid":"7d155ffe-957b-497b-a22c-9393a1b7f60b","ttft_stream_ms":3825,"time_to_request_ms":66,"first_content_fra